orow(14, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU ANSWERED ME AND SAID: THE THING YOU HAVE SPOKEN IS GOOD TO DO" (1:14) — YOU SHOULD HAVE SAID: OUR MASTER MOSES, FROM WHOM IS IT FITTING TO LEARN TORAH — FROM YOU, OR FROM YOUR DISCIPLE, OR FROM YOUR DISCIPLE\'S DISCIPLE? IS IT NOT FROM YOU, WHO SUFFERED FOR IT? AS IT SAYS "AND HE WAS THERE WITH THE LORD FORTY DAYS AND FORTY NIGHTS" (EXODUS 34:28) AND "I STAYED ON THE MOUNTAIN FORTY DAYS" (9:9). BUT I KNOW WHAT IS UNDER YOUR HEELS: YOU SAID, NOW HE WILL APPOINT OVER US EIGHTY THOUSAND JUDGES LESS A FEW, AND IF NOT I, MY SON, AND IF NOT MY SON, MY GRANDSON — AND WE WILL BRING HIM A GIFT AND HE WILL FAVOR US IN JUDGMENT. The row on 1:14 ({SP_(14, 1, "ממי", "נאה", "ללמד", "תורה")} "from whom is it fitting to learn Torah"; {SP_(14, 1, "שנצטערת", "עליה")} "who suffered for it"; {SP_(14, 1, "שמונים", "אלף")} "eighty thousand"): 9:9\'s forty days read as Moses\' SUFFERING FOR THE TORAH, quoted beside Exodus 34:28 — the two tellings of the fast (the first forty of 24:18 and the third of 34:28 joined as one; the shelf\'s count of the ascents belongs to the compile). The eighty thousand judges of 1:15 (the parallels at Sanhedrin 18a the English notes). REREAD WHOLE — first read at sitting 1 (chapters 1-3\'s piska).')
orow(25, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"CITIES GREAT AND FORTIFIED TO THE HEAVENS" (1:28) — RABBAN SHIMON BEN GAMLIEL SAYS: THE SCRIPTURES SPEAK IN HYPERBOLE, AS IT SAYS "HEAR, O ISRAEL, YOU ARE PASSING OVER THE JORDAN TODAY [TO DISPOSSESS NATIONS GREATER AND MIGHTIER THAN YOU, CITIES GREAT AND FORTIFIED TO THE HEAVENS]" (9:1); BUT WHAT THE ALL-PRESENT SAID TO ABRAHAM OUR FATHER, "I WILL MULTIPLY YOUR SEED AS THE STARS OF HEAVEN" (GENESIS 26:4), "I WILL MAKE YOUR SEED AS THE DUST OF THE EARTH" (GENESIS 13:16) — THESE ARE NOT HYPERBOLE. The row on 1:28 ({SP_(25, 4, "דברו", "כתובים", "לשון", "הביי")} "the Scriptures speak in hyperbole" — the shelf\'s own spelling of the word, asserted on its bytes): THE HYPERBOLE RULE — 9:1\'s "to the heavens" (1:28\'s phrase, spelled defective here and plene there) is Scripture\'s exaggeration, the promise to Abraham is not; Onkelos\'s "to the HEIGHT of heaven" at both seats is the same reading in the translation\'s hand (the ink). REREAD WHOLE — first read at sitting 1 and, by topic, at a Genesis sitting (gen_29 — the hyperbole rule grading 13:16 literal).')
orow(26, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "AND I BESOUGHT THE LORD" (3:23) — PRAYER IS CALLED BY TEN NAMES: CRY, SHOUT, GROAN (EXODUS 2:23-24); DISTRESS AND CALLING (2 SAMUEL 22:7); SONG AND ENTREATY (JEREMIAH 7:16); FALLING, AS IT SAYS "AND I FELL DOWN BEFORE THE LORD" (9:25); PRAYER, AS IT SAYS "AND I PRAYED TO THE LORD" (9:26); ENTREATING (GENESIS 25:21); STANDING (PSALM 106:30); IMPLORING (EXODUS 32:11); BESEECHING, AS IT SAYS "AND I BESOUGHT THE LORD". The row on 3:23 ({SP_(26, 7, "עשרה", "לשונות", "נקראת", "תפלה")} "prayer is called by ten names"; {SP_(26, 7, "נקראת", "נפול")} "called falling"; {SP_(26, 7, "נקראת", "פלול")} "called prayer"): TWO OF THE TEN NAMES ARE THIS CHAPTER\'S — 9:25\'s "fell down" (the hithpael, the Torah\'s two seats both here) and 9:26\'s "prayed" (the hithpael, the Torah\'s eight); the ninth, "imploring", is Exodus 32:11 — THE SAME PRAYER\'S FIRST TELLING (the ink: 9:26 against 32:11 five tokens shared). The English translator counts thirteen synonyms in the list and notes the reconciliation (an editorial note, not a citation). REREAD WHOLE — first read at sitting 1.')
orow(27, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "YOU HAVE BEGUN" (3:24) — YOU OPENED ME A DOOR TO STAND AND PRAY BEFORE YOU FOR YOUR SONS WHEN THEY STANK IN THE DEED OF THE CALF, AS IT SAYS "LET ME ALONE AND I WILL DESTROY THEM" (9:14) — WAS MOSES HOLDING THE HOLY ONE? RATHER, THUS HE SAID BEFORE HIM: MASTER OF THE WORLD, YOU OPENED ME A DOOR TO STAND AND PRAY FOR YOUR SONS; I STOOD AND PRAYED FOR THEM, AND YOU HEARD MY PRAYER AND FORGAVE THEIR INIQUITY. I THOUGHT I WAS WITH THEM IN PRAYER, AND THEY DID NOT PRAY FOR ME. AND IS IT NOT A MATTER OF LIGHT AND HEAVY: IF THE PRAYER OF ONE FOR THE MANY IS SO HEARD, THE PRAYER OF THE MANY FOR ONE ALL THE MORE! The row on 3:24 ({SP_(27, 2, "אתה", "פתחת", "לי", "פתח")} "You opened me a door"; {SP_(27, 2, "וכי", "משה", "תפוס", "היה", "בקדש")} "was Moses holding the Holy One?"; {SP_(27, 2, "והלא", "דברים", "קל", "וחמר")} "is it not light and heavy" — the shelf\'s own spelling): THE DOOR OPENED — 9:14\'s "let Me alone" read as an invitation to pray (Onkelos supplies the prayer in the same clause: "leave your prayer from before Me" — the ink); the a-fortiori I1 (qal wa-chomer, "light and heavy") from the one\'s prayer for the many (heard: 9:19) to the many\'s for the one (Moses\' own plea of 3:23-26, refused — the piska\'s point). REREAD WHOLE — first read at sitting 1.')
orow(306, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'ANOTHER WORD: "MY DOCTRINE SHALL DROP AS THE RAIN" (32:2) — THE SAGES SAY: MOSES SAID TO ISRAEL, PERHAPS YOU DO NOT KNOW HOW MUCH I SUFFERED FOR THE TORAH, HOW MUCH I LABORED IN IT AND WEARIED IN IT, AS IT SAYS "AND HE WAS THERE WITH THE LORD FORTY DAYS AND FORTY NIGHTS" (EXODUS 34:28) AND "I STAYED ON THE MOUNTAIN FORTY DAYS AND FORTY NIGHTS" (9:9); I WENT IN AMONG THE ANGELS, AMONG THE LIVING CREATURES, AMONG THE SERAPHIM OF WHOM ONE COULD BURN THE WHOLE WORLD (ISAIAH 6:2); I GAVE MY SOUL FOR IT, MY BLOOD FOR IT — AS I LEARNED IT IN SUFFERING SO SHALL YOU LEARN IT IN SUFFERING; OR AS YOU LEARN IT IN SUFFERING SO SHALL YOU TEACH IT IN SUFFERING? THE TEACHING SAYS "MY SPEECH SHALL DISTIL AS THE DEW" — SEE IT AS CHEAP, THREE OR FOUR SEAHS A SELA. The row on 32:2 ({SP_(306, 25, "כמה", "צער", "נצטערתי", "על", "התורה")} "how much I suffered for the Torah"; {SP_(306, 25, "נכנסתי", "לבין", "המלאכים")} "I went in among the angels"; {SP_(306, 25, "נפשי", "נתתי", "עליה")} "I gave my soul for it"): 9:9 quoted with Exodus 34:28 again (14:1\'s pair) — the forty days as the price of the Torah; THE ENGLISH MIS-CITES THE EXODUS VERSE as "Ex.36:28" (the Hebrew\'s "שמות לד כח" is 34:28; 36:28 is a tabernacle board) — a slip on the kin\'s citation, asserted on both files\' bytes; the row kept whole. Fresh.')
orow(342, 1, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND THIS IS THE BLESSING WITH WHICH MOSES BLESSED" (33:1) — SINCE MOSES SPOKE HARSH WORDS TO ISRAEL FIRST, "WASTED WITH HUNGER AND DEVOURED WITH BURNING HEAT" (32:24), "OUTSIDE THE SWORD SHALL BEREAVE" (32:25), "AT HOREB YOU PROVOKED THE LORD" (9:8), "YOU HAVE BEEN REBELLIOUS" (9:7), HE TURNED AND SPOKE WORDS OF COMFORT TO THEM: "AND THIS IS THE BLESSING". The row on 33:1 ({SP_(342, 1, "דברים", "קשים", "תחלה")} "harsh words first"; {SP_(342, 1, "ובחרב", "הקצפתם")} "at Horeb you provoked"; {SP_(342, 1, "ממרים", "הייתם")} "you have been rebellious"): 9:7-8 among the book\'s harsh words before its blessing — the Hebrew\'s RANGE citation "9:7-8" the regex does not read, the row found through the English\'s two citations (asserted). Fresh.')
orow(357, 44, 'MATERIAL', f'R. ELAZAR SAYS: "AND IN ALL THE SIGNS AND THE WONDERS" (34:11) — AND WHENCE EVEN BEFORE MOUNT SINAI? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND IN ALL THE MIGHTY HAND" (34:12); AND WHENCE EVEN IN THE WILDERNESS? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND IN ALL THE GREAT TERROR"; AND WHENCE EVEN THE BREAKING OF THE TABLETS? IT IS SAID THERE "AND I BROKE THEM BEFORE YOUR EYES" (9:17), AND HERE IT SAYS "WHICH MOSES DID BEFORE THE EYES OF ALL ISRAEL" (34:12). The row on 34:12 ({SP_(357, 44, "רבי", "אלעזר", "אומר")} "R. Elazar says"; {SP_(357, 44, "ומנין", "אף", "בשבור", "הלוחות")} "and whence even the breaking of the tablets"; {SP_(357, 44, "נאמר", "להלן")} "it is said there"; {SP_(357, 44, "וכאן", "הוא", "אומר")} "and here it says"): THE BREAKING OF THE TABLETS COUNTED AMONG MOSES\' WONDERS — the verbal analogy I2 (gezerah shavah) on "before your eyes" (9:17) and "before the eyes of all Israel" (34:12), the book\'s closing verse read through this chapter\'s; the breaking is the book\'s last word about Moses (the compile\'s row on 9:17 — Exodus 32:19\'s line, told here in Moses\' own words with one token shared). Fresh.')

